<task id="040" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-17 + NFR-04: Intake mailbox — intake flag + default request type on sprk_communicationaccount; any sender → request + run; thread reply → new run; per-sender daily cap</title>
    <phase>2 Email and Copilot doors</phase>
    <gate>after:029</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags bff-api and dataverse; modifies the inbound email processor (.cs) and adds Dataverse columns; depends on the whole Phase 1 chain via 029.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Brownfield change in a hot shared file (`IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs`, PR #1494 nearby) with redelivery and an abuse guard; a wrong gate auto-creates requests from ordinary mailboxes.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>file-overlap with 042 (processor) and 043 (DI module); 041/042 read the flag added here.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>029</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, backend, dataverse, fields, config</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-7 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make a mailbox an intake door. Add two columns to `sprk_communicationaccount` (intake flag, default request type) mapped on `CommunicationAccount`. In `IncomingCommunicationProcessor`, after normal filing, mail at an intake mailbox from ANY sender creates one request (channel Email) and one run via task 022's submit service, unless the sender is over the per-sender daily cap (default 20): then the mail is filed with no run and raises admin attention. A reply on a request's thread adds a run to that request. A non-intake mailbox never creates a request.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Spaarke inbound email pipeline (`IncomingCommunicationProcessor`, thread resolution), Dataverse schema scripts and ADR-004 idempotency. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Intake columns deployed by script and mapped; an intake step idempotent per Graph message that respects the cap and kill switch and never affects filing; tests for each FR-17 case.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-17 (a–e), NFR-04, NFR-08; owner Q7. Reuse-scan row 8: extend the inbound processor; `sprk_autocreaterecords` gates attachment filing (`:433`) and must not mean "takes requests". The processor dedups at step 1 (`:140-149`), so the intake step must stay reachable after a crash between filing and request creation. Request + run creation goes through task 022's `IntakeRequestSubmitService`. The #1920 producer at the same site is task 042.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs (account read ~:152, filing gate :433)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationAccountService.cs (select list :72, mapping ~:165)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/CommunicationAccount.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/IntakeMailboxStep.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">the intake DI module created by task 013 (registration of IntakeMailboxStep; exact name set by 013)</file>
      <file role="new">scripts/Add-IntakeMailboxColumns.ps1</file>
      <file role="modify">src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/Entities/sprk_CommunicationAccount/Entity.xml</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/data-model/sprk_communicationaccount.md</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Communication/IntakeMailboxStepTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Communication/IntakeSenderCapTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Add-BindingContextTypeTagsColumn.ps1 (add columns to an existing entity)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ThreadResolver.cs (thread join for replies)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/IntakeRequestSubmitService.cs (task 022)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/Handlers/IncomingCommunicationJobHandler.cs (job entry; touched by open PR #1494 — read only here)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="029" status="pending">Phase 1 deployed and verified (request/run records, orchestrator, submit service from 022, status emails from 020).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = the intake gate. Only an account with the new intake flag = true runs the intake step; `sprk_autocreaterecords` is not read for this decision; a non-intake mailbox never creates a request or run (FR-17 d).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = filing. The intake step runs after the existing filing steps (communication, attachment documents, .eml archive) and is best-effort with respect to them: an intake failure never fails or skips filing (FR-17 e).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">SCOPE = the intake step. Idempotent per Graph message: key `intake-email:{graphMessageId}` claimed atomically before the request is created; the step is also reached on the duplicate-detected path for intake mailboxes, so a redelivery after a crash completes it once; run payloads carry ids only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">SCOPE = the per-sender cap (the Event-path budget). Count requests with channel Email whose requester email equals the normalized (lower-case) sender created since 00:00 UTC on this stamp; at or over `Intake:Email:PerSenderDailyCap` (default 20) → no request, no run, a telemetry event `Intake.SenderCapExceeded` and a Warning log with ids only (sender hashed); the mail is still filed (FR-17 c).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">SCOPE = the email door. Kill switch `Intake:Doors:Email:Enabled` (default false) makes the intake step a no-op; filing is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">SCOPE = logs and payloads. No email body, subject, attachment bytes or sender address in logs or queue payloads; ids and a sender hash only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">SCOPE = request creation. Through `IntakeRequestSubmitService` only (channel Email, requester = matched contact/user or the sender address, owner = the intake mailbox's owning team, request type = the account's default until classification sets it, send-email-updates ON per task 020).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = shared files. `IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs` is shared with the email-communication projects; run `/conflict-check`; if PR #1494 (touches `IncomingCommunicationJobHandler.cs`) merges first, rebase over it. Dataverse schema changes on dev need the owner's OK.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE = this task's BFF changes. State the Placement Justification in the PR (`.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build (total ≤ 60 MB); no new package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
