      <pattern name="Plugin structure" location=".claude/patterns/dataverse/plugin-structure.md">Tag-mapped; no plugin is added (ADR-002).</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load the knowledge files; read the processor end to end (dedup, account lookup, filing, DocAnalysis enqueue ~:1640) and ThreadResolver; check PR #1494's state; declare RIGOR FULL, tier opus, effort high.</step>
    <step order="2">Write `scripts/Add-IntakeMailboxColumns.ps1` (copy `Add-BindingContextTypeTagsColumn.ps1`): `sprk_isintakemailbox` (Yes/No, default No) and `sprk_intakedefaultrequesttype` (Choice, same values as `sprk_servicerequest.sprk_requesttype`); update Entity.xml and the data-model doc. Run on dev only with the owner's OK.</step>
    <step order="3">Map the columns on `CommunicationAccount` and add them to the account select list(s).</step>
    <step order="4">Write `IntakeMailboxStep.RunAsync(account, communicationId, graphMessageId, sender, ct)`: kill switch → thread check (reply to a communication that is a request's regarding communication → new run on that request) → cap → create request + run via `IntakeRequestSubmitService`; all under the idempotency key.</step>
    <step order="5">Call it from the processor after filing for intake accounts, and from the duplicate-detected path for intake accounts.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests per the criteria (data-mutation for the step, domain unit for the cap rule); build and run tests; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="8">Document deviations (final column names) in projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Before running the schema script on dev, STOP and get the owner's explicit OK (project CLAUDE.md §5).</trigger>
    <trigger>If the thread resolution cannot tell a reply on a request's thread from a new mail without reading the body, STOP and escalate rather than matching on subject text (ADR-015, and fuzzy matching would misroute).</trigger>
    <trigger>If PR #1494 or another project has uncommitted changes to the same processor methods, STOP and coordinate before editing.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row 8: `IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs:152` (gate `:433`), `CommunicationAccountService.cs:165` (columns `:72`), `CommunicationAccount` model; the closest flag `sprk_autocreaterecords` gates filing. spec New Components row "Intake flag on sprk_communicationaccount".</existing>
    <extension>The processor and account model are extended. New columns are needed because neither `sprk_autocreaterecords` (filing) nor `sprk_accounttype` (owner kind) means "this mailbox takes requests"; overloading them would change filing for existing mailboxes. `IntakeMailboxStep` is a separate class so the 2,000-line processor gains one call, not a second responsibility.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Mail sent to the legal mailbox never becomes a request, so the email door (FR-17, success criterion 6) does not exist; without the cap, any sender could trigger unbounded AI runs (NFR-04).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Schema script</tool>
  </tools>

