  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A new mail at an intake mailbox from any sender creates exactly one request (channel Email) and one run (FR-17 a).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A reply on that request's thread creates a second run on the same request and no new request (FR-17 b).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The sender's mail over the daily cap is filed, creates no request or run, and emits `Intake.SenderCapExceeded` (FR-17 c); the cap value comes from configuration (default 20).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: mail at a non-intake mailbox (including one with `sprk_autocreaterecords` = true) creates no request or run (FR-17 d).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Normal filing (communication, attachment documents, .eml archive) happens for every mail, including over-cap and intake-failure cases (FR-17 e).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Redelivering the same Graph message (including after a simulated crash between filing and request creation) yields exactly one request and one run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With the email kill switch off, no request or run is created and filing is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No log or payload contains the body, subject, attachment bytes or sender address.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The schema script is idempotent (re-run is a no-op) and the data-model doc lists both columns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build and all tests pass; the PR states the Placement Justification and publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE). Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative cases named above; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes. One seeding proof for the non-intake gate.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-17, NFR-04. Column names are proposals; record the final names in notes and the data-model doc.</notes>

